# Scoring model: one source of truth, two languages

`ai/pipeline/scoring.py` (seed generation / live worker) and
`backend/internal/domain/lighting/model/scoring.go` (backend live scoring +
simulation) are **deterministic ports of each other**.

## When you change one, change both

- Keep `RECOMMENDED_DENSITY`, `ROAD_WEIGHT`, thresholds, and the risk formula
  byte-for-byte equivalent.
- Update the Go unit tests in `scoring_test.go` to lock the new behavior.
- Mismatches cause precomputed seeds and live analysis to disagree — a demo bug.

```go
// Go and Python must produce the same risk_score for the same inputs.
ScoreSegment(streetlights, lengthM, roadType, nightRatio)
```
